preConditionHook:
// THIS BAR IS AN OUTSIDE BAR AND THE BAR BEFORE IT WAS NOT A DECENT SIGNAL
// BAR. Brooks: a reversal entry on an outside bar needs a decent signal bar
// ahead of it, so the composite is carried whole and stated in the FAILING
// sense -- place it NEGATED to demand the signal bar, or leave it as written
// to block the setup.
//
// Carried whole because the negation of an AND is an OR, which two ANDed entry
// panes cannot express (SmallWeakSignalBarBlock is the same shape).
//
// OUTSIDE BAR is the strict two-sided engulf OutsideOutsidePattern uses, read
// at lag 0: high[0] > high[1] and low[0] < low[1].
//
// DECENT BULL REVERSAL BAR (the half that is negated): the prior bar closed
// above its own open AND closed within closeNearFraction of its own high. The
// short side mirrors it -- a bear body closing within closeNearFraction of its
// own low. This is CloseRangePosition's measurement combined with a body SIGN
// and read one bar back, which is why neither pane supplies it.
//
// Products, not quotients: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero and a
// zero-range bar is legal data.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 1.
